&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;The PPTX figures below are for v0.5.0 and the vector PDF figures for v0.4.0.
The first table is for v0.3.0,
the previous release, which renders slides concurrently and parses its fonts
once (&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-slides/slides/pull/11" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;go-slides/slides#11&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;go-slides and &lt;a href="https://github.com/marp-team/marp-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;marp-cli&lt;/a&gt; 4.5.1 were
run as subprocesses on the same decks, on an Apple M4 Max (16 CPUs) with a
1-minute load average under 8, five interleaved rounds after a warm-up.
Time is the median wall time; memory is the peak of the whole process tree
(marp-cli drives a Chrome, whose processes count).&lt;/p&gt;
